Description: AI companion for KDE Plasma 6 with AI usage meters and AI chats
 Hearthwire sits in the KDE Plasma 6 panel. Its Chat tab opens AI chat sites
 (Claude, ChatGPT, Grok, Gemini, GitHub Copilot, Microsoft Copilot, a local
 web UI) or a built-in chat with local Ollama models, private by default.
 Its Usage tab shows how much of each AI coding plan is left (Claude Code,
 Codex, Cursor, Antigravity, GitHub Copilot, Devin, Grok), read by a small
 Python helper that uses only the standard library.
 .
 The Chat tab needs Qt WebEngine (recommended). Stay signed in needs
 gocryptfs, fuse3 and kdialog; Unlock with KDE Wallet also needs kwallet6,
 qdbus-qt6 and openssl. The Ollama chat needs Ollama, which Ubuntu does not
 package.
